{"author":{"id":"2462ded6f56967dde059994c39a506c79e39e5dfd10c5a07f07a23a5652a8353"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773780641,"nonce":"gccEe06LwiGpjOHQ/G43nDHFExQ=","title":"Watcher should pass --workflow to all launch.py invocations","message":"The watcher receives `--workflow` and stores it in `SessionMonitor.workflow_path`, but two code paths that spawn `launch.py` don't pass it through:\n\n1. **`_resume_session()`** (line ~140) — only passes `--workflow` for review sessions (`REVIEW.md`), not for regular coder sessions.\n2. **`check_new_issues()`** (line ~344) — auto-start never passes `--workflow` at all.\n\nBoth rely on default discovery (`.nightshift.yaml` or `WORKFLOW.md` in repo root), which breaks when the workflow file is at a custom location specified via `nightshift init --workflow-path`.\n\n**Fix:** In both `_resume_session()` and `check_new_issues()`, append `[\"--workflow\", str(self.workflow_path)]` to the `cmd` list before calling `_launch_background()`. For review sessions, keep the existing `REVIEW.md` override.\n\n**Tests needed:**\n- Assert `--workflow` appears in the launched command for orphan resume\n- Assert `--workflow` appears in the launched command for auto-start\n- Assert review sessions still get `REVIEW.md` override when it exists","files":null}]}